kosha partial-derivative

  -- partial-derivative: kramanusara of a multi-variable expression
  -- w.r.t. one apeksha variable, all others held constant (treated as sthira-apeksha)
  -- d(f)/d(x_j) where x_0..x_{n-1} are inputs and only x_j is the apeksha

  "kramanusara-swarupa derivative-abheda"
  "apeksha-yukta viveka-siddha"
  "aneka-ahara eka-apeksha-phala"
  -- x_j (the differentiation variable) is the chala-apeksha — it is the one that varies
  -- all other x_i (i≠j) become sthira-apeksha — held constant, frozen as fixed reference
  "chala-apeksha-siddha sthira-apeksha-yukta"
  "jacobian-janaka gradient-janaka"
  "domain-math-sthita"

